This file refers to the paging device in use by the system.  This
may  actually be a subdevice of one of the disk drivers, but in a
system with paging interleaved across  multiple  disk  drives  it
provides an indirect driver for the multiple drives.  The special
file  appeared  in Reads from the drum are not allowed across the
interleaving boundaries.  Since these only occur  every  .5Mbytes
or  so,  and  since  the system never allocates blocks across the
boundary, this is usually not a problem.
